From fde1ba22f6761af14d706994ab53df408674d900 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:10:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: stranded-park: bound the stale-sweep
 deferral

- A card that keeps getting events (comments) is never idle for
  sweep_stale_triage, so waiting on that sweep deferred it forever. The wait now
  lasts only while the park episode is younger than
  kanban.stranded_stale_defer_seconds (21600); after that the card is escalated
  even if stale triage has not run.
- awaiting_stale_sweep is false for a card with any stored human_request: the
  stale sweep skips those, so an invalid request is the stranded sweep's to
  replace (it judges asks with card_is_open_human_ask).

Co-Authored-By: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
